Graber1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Graber</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Cantor</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohr</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Genomic detection of new yeast pre-mRNA 3&#x02032;-end-processing signals.</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><volume>27</volume><fpage>888</fpage><lpage>894</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9889288</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000290-Graber2"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Graber</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>McAllister</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Probabilistic prediction of Saccharomyces cerevisiae mRNA 3&#x02032;-processing sites.</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>1851</fpage><lpage>1858</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11937640</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000290-vanHelden1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Helden</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>del Olmo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Perez-Ortin</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Statistical analysis of yeast genomic downstream sequences reveals putative polyadenylation signals.</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><volume>28</volume><fpage>1000</fpage><lpage>1010</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10648794</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000290-Kellis1"><label>13</label><citation citation-ty